id: pm-rust-crash-harness
title: Compare native and published crash recovery with a reusable kill corpus
description: "Reusable TypeScript process-kill/restart differential SDK and command against the locked published oracle; compare acknowledged durable bytes, append-only histories and restart receipts on disposable plain-directory trackers."
type: Feature
status: open
priority: 2
tags[3]: conformance,crash-consistency,harness
created_at: "2026-10-21T21:59:35.474Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-25T07:26:31.736Z"
author: codex-agent
acceptance_criteria: Every declared crash boundary preserves acknowledged writes; failures retain minimized synthetic reproductions and never rewrite original history.; Typed SDK and CLI with bounded TOON/JSON receipts and actionable refusals; documented example; public tracker read-copy validation with measured counts; exact-head CI release-check passes.
unblock_note: Native cross-operation recovery is integrated from main and both live permanent replays pass with zero pending journals and successful return operations.
comments[40]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-21T21:59:37.843Z",codex-agent,"Overlap recheck: published CLI 2026.10.21 matches the locked oracle. Native tests cover normal command differentials and manually reconstructed durable journals; they do not run a reusable live kill/restart corpus. pm-ops assurance reports measurements; pm-vcs writer publication is backend-specific. This feature adds cross-implementation crash evidence beyond lock/parity work. Reconciliation PR 103 closures and performance PR 102 items are excluded. TypeScript-only SDK/command; synthetic failures; targeted local checks; full gate in CI."
  "2026-10-21T22:16:09.535Z",codex-agent,"Implemented the typed TypeScript SDK and standalone just crash CLI. Declared boundaries are all observed rename/fsync task-local ordinals: event-loop write calls were rejected as unstable storage boundaries after real tracing. Two mutation families run on disposable non-git clones; same-family restart checks exact durable bytes and raw per-runtime restart receipts, with explicit shared cross-runtime acknowledgement projections. Synthetic probing measured 20 real kills, 20 preserved acknowledged writes/history prefixes, two successful baseline byte/acknowledgement comparisons and two early native lock-initialization restart refusals. Those refusals are retained as minimal one-item synthetic cases; no original stream is repaired. Full runtime crash conformance is not claimed. Adding independent replay/no-git regressions and public-copy measurements before CI."
  "2026-10-21T22:19:48.804Z",codex-agent,"Read-only public-copy validation: public main c0154dbd7cd8071ac52b891be13f956f7a0f21fd, 74 items and 154 authoritative files in a non-git copy with read-only permissions. Measured 20 injected kills, 20 acknowledged-write preservations, 20 exact retained-history prefixes, two cross-runtime baseline byte/acknowledgement matches, 18 successful restart state/receipt checks, two independently reproduced native incomplete-lock restart refusals. Source fingerprint unchanged. Retained evidence is synthetic only. Follow-up pm-rust-crash-lock-restart covers the safe recovery policy, outside this harness change. Behavioral controls disabling history-prefix checking, exact inventory comparison and injected-kill admission each fail their targeted regression with exit 1 and pass after exact byte restoration."
  "2026-10-21T22:21:46.519Z",codex-agent,"Final targeted checks: pinned PM linked runner passes 14/14 Node regressions with no skips, including real native/published kills, read-only source-output guards, a PATH with no git executable, and independent one-case replay. Strict erasable TypeScript typecheck, ESLint, Rust fmt and targeted binary Clippy pass. Four behavioral negative controls now fail independently and pass after byte restoration, including rejecting a successful restart that lost its own history. Full unchanged-threshold Rust release-check is reserved for CI; no local full release suite was run. Local health retains existing guidance/provenance/stale-item advisories and shared configuration drift; history was not repaired. CI uses its existing clone-local configuration setup. Full CI run results and exact counts will be linked in the PR."
  "2026-10-22T10:38:52.442Z",codex-agent,"PR 104 review round: pulled remote head and merged origin/main. PRRT_kwDOTwgMRs6vBg8Y is valid: oracle metadata read/parse errors bypass oracle_version. Adding public SDK/CLI regressions for missing, unreadable, malformed, invalid-shape and wrong-version metadata. Full-diff self-review found the same parse-before-typed-refusal pattern in mutation acknowledgements: malformed successful stdout bypasses baseline_failed. Covering and correcting that instance too. Replay-manifest parsing already has its typed invalid_options catch. Latest substantive CodeRabbit review has no Outside diff range findings. No thread replies or resolutions."
  "2026-10-22T10:42:18.350Z",codex-agent,"Full-diff validation review also found malformed source settings JSON bypassed its unsafe_source guard. Corrected all three parse-before-validation paths: oracle metadata maps to oracle_version, source settings to unsafe_source, and malformed successful mutation stdout to baseline_failed. Added ten SDK oracle metadata cases, bounded JSON/default CLI refusal checks, source immutability checks and a real published-CLI baseline with an incompatible executable. No PM SDK mocks; all fixtures are disposable non-git directories. Replay-manifest parsing already preserves invalid_options. Original histories and all gate thresholds remain unchanged."
  "2026-10-22T10:43:02.665Z",codex-agent,"Independent revert proofs complete with exact source-byte restoration. Oracle metadata: replacing only its guarded read/parse with the original statement makes both SDK and CLI regressions fail (2/2, io_error); restored both pass. Source settings: reverting only its guarded parse fails 1/1 with io_error; restored passes 1/1. Mutation acknowledgement: reverting only its guarded parse fails 1/1 with io_error; restored passes 1/1 using real published init/create processes and an incompatible native executable. Exact commands: node --test --test-name-pattern=\"oracle metadata\" scripts/crash-harness.test.mts; node --test --test-name-pattern=\"malformed source settings\" scripts/crash-harness.test.mts; node --test --test-name-pattern=\"malformed mutation acknowledgements\" scripts/crash-harness.test.mts. Each negative run exits 1 from the intended assertion; each restored run exits 0."
  "2026-10-22T10:44:51.308Z",codex-agent,"Final local targeted validation passed: strict erasable TypeScript compiler and ESLint checks; full crash harness 18/18 with zero skips; linked new regressions 4/4. All three independent behavior reverts failed exactly their intended assertions (2+1+1), then passed restored (2+1+1). Isolated pinned-PM health passed. Starting unchanged-threshold just release-check with the existing 35-minute release CI budget as the local wall-time bound."
  "2026-10-22T10:56:48.191Z",codex-agent,"Local full release attempt is incomplete, not failed: dependency install, fmt, strict Clippy and private-item rustdoc passed; the cold Rust test build was stopped under shared-host contention (main compiler about 7 percent CPU over six minutes). No compiler or test assertion failed. Using exact-head CI for the full unchanged-threshold release gate; this PR remains the active round until that gate passes. Targeted TypeScript compiler/lint checks, full Linux crash harness 18/18, linked new controls 4/4 and all independent revert proofs already pass."
  "2026-10-22T11:23:46.735Z",codex-agent,"Full CI release evidence at code head 5b84803625d18e3ab3b7fdb4454a49448a628bf6: Linux just release-check passed (https://github.com/unbraind/pm-rust/actions/runs/39767043319/job/119784971422). Ordinary and instrumented Rust tests each passed 578 across 22 suites, zero failed or ignored; Rust lines 14025/14025, functions 1466/1466, regions 23438/23438, branches 3296/3296, all 100 percent. TypeScript compiler, ESLint and Linux crash harness 18/18 with zero skips also passed inside the gate. Audit, changelog and strict tracker health passed; only the pre-existing allowed RUSTSEC-2024-0449 advisory remains. macOS full release gate also passed: 567 ordinary and 567 instrumented Rust tests; all four required Rust metrics 100 percent; Node harness 11 passed with 7 declared Linux-only skips. The stopped local cold-build attempt is incomplete evidence; CI supplies the full pass. Releasing the claim and retaining in_progress for orchestrator verification. Final receipt-head CI evidence will be linked from PR 104; no thread replies/resolutions, PR merge or release."
  "2026-10-22T16:37:02.495Z",codex-agent,"New PR 104 review round: pulled remote head 328ff00, then merged origin/main a600bd8 because the branch was one commit behind. Thread PRRT_kwDOTwgMRs6vRw2E is valid: the retained-case example claims every replay selects one implementation/syscall/ordinal, but baseline_parity evidence reruns its scenario across both implementations and all observed boundaries. The public SDK replay docstring has the same overstatement. Will correct both descriptions and add a regression tied to the replay contract with a documentation revert proof. Latest CodeRabbit review has no Outside diff range findings. Existing implementation, completed review fixes and append-only histories remain intact."
  "2026-10-22T16:41:16.374Z",codex-agent,"Documentation revert proof for PRRT_kwDOTwgMRs6vRw2E: node --test --test-name-pattern=\"replay guidance\" scripts/crash-harness.test.mts checks the public guide and SDK docstring. Reverting only docs/CRASH_HARNESS.md yields one intended missing-baseline_parity-exception failure and one unaffected pass. Restoring it and reverting only the replay API docstring yields the other intended failure and one unaffected pass. Both exact byte sequences restored: 2/2 pass. These are documentation-contract controls; runtime replay behavior was already correct and was not changed. The complete just crash-check passes strict erasable TypeScript, ESLint and 20/20 Linux tests with zero failed/canceled/skipped; current native build also passes. Pinned-PM linked controls pass 2/2; result storage remains disabled by project policy, so results are retained here."
  "2026-10-22T16:41:17.977Z",codex-agent,"Self-review of the whole PR confirms the only overstatements were the retained-case guide and public replay docstring; README, CLI help, manifest validation and the single-boundary selection type do not claim that every replay selects one case. Original histories, stored commands and implementation behavior remain untouched. Releasing the implementation claim with status retained in_progress. Final exact-head unchanged just release-check CI receipts and counts will be recorded in PR https://github.com/unbraind/pm-rust/pull/104; pending CI is not approval. The original stacked-PR instruction still requires merging this completed update and main into PR 105 after PR 104 has passed and been pushed. No review replies/resolutions, PR merge or release."
  "2026-10-22T16:47:29.332Z",codex-agent,"Additional self-review caught an LF-only assumption in the new guide regression. The matcher now accepts both LF and CRLF and exercises both spellings using the real guide contents. Reverting only the optional carriage-return matcher makes the CRLF assertion fail; restoring it passes both guidance tests 2/2. Strict TypeScript and ESLint pass. No documentation, runtime function, input fixture or gate threshold changed in this follow-up. Superseded pending CI at 84ddc56 is not used as approval; the corrected final head needs fresh full release CI."
  "2026-10-24T21:48:10.764Z",codex-agent,"Returned to open in the 2026-10-24 sweep: Open PR https://github.com/unbraind/pm-rust/pull/104 carries the reusable kill-corpus harness; merged PR 105 fixes lock recovery but is not complete harness delivery. Review and full harness acceptance remain pending, with no active agent established."
  "2026-10-25T02:26:08.451Z",codex-agent,"Orchestrator correction: restored this item and its history exactly from main before writing. Main records remain untouched. Branch-only intended evidence is now re-recorded through the pinned CLI as new events, not copied or spliced. The prior archive-based resolution was rejected and is superseded by this linear main-chain extension. Runtime implementation and previously completed crash acceptance remain unchanged; adding a PR-wide byte-prefix regression and fresh health/CI evidence."
  "2026-10-25T02:26:24.823Z",codex-agent,"Historical branch evidence from 2026-10-23T06:38:11.820Z, re-recorded after main-chain restoration; later corrections supersede earlier approaches: Orchestrator review follow-up on PR 104: remote f555a42 was current; merged main c46ad00 and preserved both benchmark and crash recipes in two overlap resolutions. Reusing this item, without redoing completed refusal/doc fixes. Will capture runtime journals, add cross-operation restart plus a return-to-original-operation probe, inject published history-open failures, compare recovered runtime outcomes, disclose clock semantics, keep replay unconditional, preserve measured failure when synthetic reduction refuses, and record reproducible source/toolchain/control artifacts. Native cross-operation repair remains a separate blocking defect unless safely implemented. No review replies or mentions."
  "2026-10-25T02:26:26.192Z",codex-agent,"Historical branch evidence from 2026-10-23T06:44:41.257Z, re-recorded after main-chain restoration; later corrections supersede earlier approaches: Confirmed blocking cross-operation journal defect with real update rename-1 kill: restart comment exits 0 while journal persists, returning to update exits 2. Created pm-rust-cross-operation-journal as priority-0 blocking Issue linked to PR 104; no Rust recovery fix is folded into this TypeScript harness change. History-path openat injection also proves published item/history divergence with exit-0 restart. Historical 20-boundary receipts remain immutable and are no longer described as complete crash evidence."
  "2026-10-25T02:26:27.405Z",codex-agent,"Historical branch evidence from 2026-10-23T06:52:47.487Z, re-recorded after main-chain restoration; later corrections supersede earlier approaches: Targeted validation now confirms update cross-operation replay and reduction-refusal CLI behavior, with clock disclosure assertions. Permanent manifests replace conditional replay coverage. Runtime snapshots retain canonical transaction JSON plus raw runtime frames; unpublished temporary files remain observed but are not misclassified as committed journals. Shared recovery comparisons fail on byte, receipt projection, state or pending-journal mismatches, and unpaired cuts are not counted. Next commit pins the code source for the reproducible control recorder; complete regressions and gate evidence remain pending."
  "2026-10-25T02:26:28.388Z",codex-agent,"Historical branch evidence from 2026-10-23T07:03:34.150Z, re-recorded after main-chain restoration; later corrections supersede earlier approaches: Review follow-up: exact behavioral controls independently failed when runtime snapshots, different-operation restart, history-open interruption, recovery comparison, clock disclosure or secondary-refusal preservation was reverted; each passed after exact restoration. Source commit 5bdcd8e records the production implementation. Expanded public read-copy validation and permanent independent replays are in progress. PR 104 is draft because priority-zero pm-rust-cross-operation-journal remains unresolved; this is storage recovery testing of our own processes in scratch trackers."
  "2026-10-25T02:26:29.435Z",codex-agent,"Historical branch evidence from 2026-10-23T07:09:28.604Z, re-recorded after main-chain restoration; later corrections supersede earlier approaches: Public-copy validation exposed nondeterministic published cache renames: libuv can place the second rename on another worker, making an observed per-thread ordinal unreachable on replay. Published rename tracing now selects only the probe item path; a separate history-open cut still interrupts after item publication. Derived cache publication is explicitly outside the corpus. A real two-publication process regression covers path scoping. The recorder checkpoints completed controls, uses a bounded 60-second public-copy process deadline and refreshes controls whose source changed."
  "2026-10-25T02:26:30.387Z",codex-agent,"Historical branch evidence from 2026-10-24T23:22:18.387Z, re-recorded after main-chain restoration; later corrections supersede earlier approaches: Resuming PR 104 in its existing worktree. Preserving unpublished commits and unfinished review fixes before merging current main. The prior 18-test receipt is historical: expanded cross-operation, journal, history-open, clock and reduction controls require fresh local and exact-head CI evidence. Full native release-check will run in CI under host contention. Acceptance will be evaluated against measured results; no merge or release."
  "2026-10-25T02:26:31.421Z",codex-agent,"Historical branch evidence from 2026-10-24T23:23:08.977Z, re-recorded after main-chain restoration; later corrections supersede earlier approaches: Main integration preserves newer native lock recovery, cross-operation journal recovery, bounded reads, adapter ABI, npm/Bun release workflows and changelog behavior alongside the expanded harness. Shared history prefixes were verified byte-identical and longer streams retained unchanged. Independently created cross-operation reports used one id; main owns the implemented task and its untouched history, while the original report and raw history are preserved byte-for-byte under docs/controls/crash-review/original-journal-report.{toon,jsonl}. No history records were rewritten. Recovery controls will now require the integrated fixes to succeed; published history-open failures remain measured, not hidden."
  "2026-10-25T02:26:32.403Z",codex-agent,"Historical branch evidence from 2026-10-24T23:25:45.396Z, re-recorded after main-chain restoration; later corrections supersede earlier approaches: After the merge, both permanent native cross-operation replays pass with zero pending journals and successful return operations. Their real child argument logs enforce the different-operation restart; first-fsync fixtures from main are retained. Corrected unfinished destination-path rename filtering after a real strace probe proved it observes no rename. Published children now use UV_THREADPOOL_SIZE=1 and retain all observed rename/fsync cuts plus history-open cuts; a real two-publication regression and independent environment revert enforce reproducibility. Compiler and ESLint pass. Local tracker health is blocked only by shared extension version skew, so isolated clone-local health and CI will supply authoritative gate evidence."
  "2026-10-25T02:26:33.390Z",codex-agent,"Historical branch evidence from 2026-10-24T23:28:19.587Z, re-recorded after main-chain restoration; later corrections supersede earlier approaches: Fresh behavioral revert proof: node scripts/crash-review-proof.mts independently disables single-worker scheduling, runtime snapshot capture, different-operation restart, history-open admission, paired recovery comparison, clock disclosure and secondary-refusal preservation. All seven negative runs exit 1 from their targeted regression, all seven exact restorations exit 0, with original source bytes verified after each. Patches and source hashes are retained under docs/controls/crash-review. Native runtime recovery remains inherited unchanged from main. The published divergence follow-up is pm-rust-published-history-open."
  "2026-10-25T02:26:34.419Z",codex-agent,"Historical branch evidence from 2026-10-24T23:31:06.778Z, re-recorded after main-chain restoration; later corrections supersede earlier approaches: Review findings PRRT_kwDOTwgMRs6vW0BC, PRRT_kwDOTwgMRs6vW0BM and PRRT_kwDOTwgMRs6vW0BU are valid. Replay/source options now use presence checks; default output includes baseline parity and actionable case/recovery failure details; completed reference and killed workspaces are removed during the run. Added real CLI and live-process scratch-budget regressions, with independent behavioral controls in the recorder. Fresh public-copy evidence measures 26 kills, 26 acknowledged-write preservations, 26 history-prefix preservations, 24 successful local recovery cases, two published history-open divergences, four cross-runtime outcome mismatches and four minimized synthetic reproductions. Source fingerprint is unchanged. Harness correctness and package gates are distinct from runtime recovery conformance."
  "2026-10-25T02:26:35.351Z",codex-agent,"Historical branch evidence from 2026-10-24T23:35:01.614Z, re-recorded after main-chain restoration; later corrections supersede earlier approaches: Preservation audit confirms all 85 main history streams remain byte-identical prefixes; both independently created original defect artifacts are byte-identical to their saved branch snapshots. Targeted native cross_operation_journal tests pass 9/9 and isolated-HOME check-only strict health passes. The evidence recorder emits applicable control patches without trailing whitespace and retains exact source/toolchain hashes. Final full harness and linked commands will run after all negative-control source bytes are restored."
  "2026-10-25T02:26:36.235Z",codex-agent,"Historical branch evidence from 2026-10-24T23:45:23.540Z, re-recorded after main-chain restoration; later corrections supersede earlier approaches: Linked execution passed commands 1, 2, 3 and 5: 22/22 harness tests, 4/4 typed refusal regressions, 2/2 replay guidance regressions and 9/9 native journal tests. The expanded combined suite hit the runner default 120-second outer budget after its first file passed 22/22; no assertion failed. Retrying only that combined command with --timeout 300. Per-test process deadlines, CI aggregate timeout, coverage thresholds and scope are unchanged. Result tracking remains disabled by project policy; evidence is recorded in comments."
  "2026-10-25T02:26:37.176Z",codex-agent,"Historical branch evidence from 2026-10-24T23:49:09.238Z, re-recorded after main-chain restoration; later corrections supersede earlier approaches: Final local acceptance: all five linked commands pass, totaling 71 test executions including repeated subsets (22 + 4 + 2 + 34 + 9). The complete Linux crash suite passes 34/34, zero failed/canceled/skipped, in 166 seconds under the 300-second outer runner budget. The old 120-second outer-budget interruption remains explicit; individual test/process deadlines and all native release/coverage gates are unchanged. Strict erasable TypeScript, ESLint, native build, targeted Clippy, fmt, isolated strict health and changelog generation/check pass. All 11 behavioral controls plus receipt-schema control fail when independently reverted and pass after exact byte restoration. The final receipt pins source commit 881f550 and all recorded source bytes match that commit. Full exact-head npm and Bun native release-check CI is the remaining readiness gate; its URL and measured counts will be recorded in PR 104."
  "2026-10-25T02:26:38.189Z",codex-agent,"Historical branch evidence from 2026-10-24T23:51:13.307Z, re-recorded after main-chain restoration; later corrections supersede earlier approaches: Source candidate acc8ca5 is pushed with a clean worktree. No automatic synchronize CI run appeared, so the existing full CI workflow was explicitly dispatched at the feature branch. A final receipt commit records the independent follow-up test; implementation, tests and hashed source remain byte-identical to 881f550. The final pushed receipt head still requires its own full native npm/Bun matrix before readiness. Exact run URL and pass counts are linked from https://github.com/unbraind/pm-rust/pull/104; pending, canceled or superseded runs are not approval. Claim remains released and item in progress."
  "2026-10-25T02:26:39.331Z",codex-agent,"Historical branch evidence from 2026-10-24T23:52:57.403Z, re-recorded after main-chain restoration; later corrections supersede earlier approaches: Merged the new tracker-only main sweep e9b88ab. The installed driver generated a re-anchored union for this divergent stream; that generated output was discarded before commit. Original canonical branch history is restored unchanged, and main status-sweep item/history bytes are preserved exactly under docs/controls/crash-review/main-status-sweep-harness.{toon,jsonl}. All other newer main statuses are retained. Implementation, tests and receipt source hashes are unchanged. Current source remains locally validated; superseded queued CI was canceled. Regenerating changelog inside this merge and requiring a fresh full matrix on the integrated head."
  "2026-10-25T02:26:41.000Z",codex-agent,"Historical branch evidence from 2026-10-25T00:07:31.755Z, re-recorded after main-chain restoration; later corrections supersede earlier approaches: Final format audit found duplicate default TOON keys when multiple failures were emitted. Strict parsing with the locked published dependency rejects that output. Extracted a typed formatter with bounded failures and recovery_failures tables, preserved case/parity details and secondary-refusal remedies, and added strict decode coverage over the measured 26-case public receipt plus the real standalone CLI. A dedicated behavioral revert restores repeated root failure keys and must fail strict decoding. JSON behavior is unchanged. Superseded CI was canceled; fresh formatter/control/full-suite evidence and exact-head CI are required before readiness."
  "2026-10-25T02:26:42.044Z",codex-agent,"Historical branch evidence from 2026-10-25T00:14:05.953Z, re-recorded after main-chain restoration; later corrections supersede earlier approaches: Final corrected local acceptance passes all five linked commands: 22 + 4 + 2 + 35 + 9 = 72 test executions including repeated subsets, zero failures or skips. The complete 35-test Linux suite passes in 131 seconds under its 300-second outer runner budget. Strict TypeScript and ESLint pass. The default CLI and the measured multi-failure receipt both decode with the locked strict TOON parser. Reverting only strict failure-table formatting restores duplicate keys and fails the new regression; restoring exact source bytes passes. All 12 behavior controls plus the receipt-schema control fail independently and pass restored. Refreshed public-copy validation at main e9b88ab measures 85 items, 176 files, 26 kills, 26 acknowledged-write preservations, 26 history-prefix preservations, 24 successful local recoveries, two published divergences, four paired mismatches and four synthetic reproductions; source unchanged. Source commit 3b0b53b and every recorded source hash match exactly. Old CI runs are superseded; final pushed-head counts will be linked from PR 104."
  "2026-10-25T02:26:43.266Z",codex-agent,"Historical branch evidence from 2026-10-25T00:36:02.940Z, re-recorded after main-chain restoration; later corrections supersede earlier approaches: CI run 40145918742 exposed a Windows-only clock-launcher failure: Node --import rejects raw drive-letter paths with ERR_UNSUPPORTED_ESM_URL_SCHEME. Windows ordinary native tests passed before the Node clock assertion; the aggregate stopped before coverage. Linux ordinary tests passed 648/648 and macOS 635/635, zero failed or ignored, but that superseded run is not final approval. The process adapter now exports a file-URL preload specifier used by both the published adapter and the real clock test. The test asserts the portable URL contract before launching the child; reverting to a raw path fails on Linux too. Clock semantics, platform skips, Rust source and all gate thresholds remain unchanged. Recording the new independent revert control, refreshing source provenance and rerunning the linked full harness before fresh exact-head CI."
  "2026-10-25T02:26:44.833Z",codex-agent,"Historical branch evidence from 2026-10-25T00:41:09.756Z, re-recorded after main-chain restoration; later corrections supersede earlier approaches: Portable-clock correction validated: all six linked commands pass (22 + 4 + 2 + 35 + 9 + 1 = 73 test executions including repeated subsets), zero failed/canceled/skipped. Full Linux suite passes 35/35 in 87 seconds; strict TypeScript and ESLint pass. The clock preload now uses a file URL in both actual launcher sites; independent raw-path reversion fails the portable URL assertion and exact restoration passes the real child clock checks. All 13 behavioral controls plus receipt-schema control fail independently and pass restored. Fresh source provenance pins 5f6664f; public-copy measurements remain 85 items, 176 files, 26 kills, all 26 acknowledged writes/history prefixes preserved, two published divergences, four paired mismatches, four synthetic reproductions and source unchanged. Prior Windows CI clock failure and all superseded runs remain historical, not approval. Fresh exact pushed-head full npm/Bun CI and counts are required and will be linked from PR 104."
  "2026-10-25T02:32:00.645Z",codex-agent,"Append-only correction complete: main item/history restored exactly, then 19 branch-only evidence comments and intended files/docs/tests/unblock rationale were re-recorded through the pinned CLI. Main records remain a byte-identical prefix. All existing main history streams pass the prefix audit; the branch-only oracle item was preserved unchanged. Added scripts/crash-history-prefix.mts to the release gate; it checks every changed history path, rejects replaced or deleted main bytes, and permits new item streams. New real-Git/PM fixture tests pass 2/2, including a plain tracker without a Git executable. Behavioral revert proof: disabling only the byte-prefix rejection yields exit 1 from the intended missing-exception assertion; exact source restoration passes 2/2. TypeScript and ESLint pass. A stale clone-only receipt from the rejected merge was quarantined outside active metadata, without repair/force/re-anchor; isolated-HOME pinned health passes with exit 0, ok true and no failing checks. Completed runtime crash/revert evidence is retained; only new prefix/health validation is rerun locally, with full exact-head CI still required."
  "2026-10-25T02:35:59.401Z",codex-agent,"Final pre-push audit: all 86 history streams present on main are byte-identical prefixes of their branch files; one branch-only oracle stream is unchanged. Main harness history has 37 original records, all preserved before the new PM events. The targeted linked prefix regression passes 2/2 with no failures, skips or empty runs. Default strict pinned health passes in isolated HOME; no active clone receipt remains. The optional full history audit reports existing mismatches for pm-rust-bj7a and pm-rust-unih; both item/history pairs are byte-for-byte identical to main and were left untouched. No main records or hash anchors were repaired. Completed runtime evidence is retained; the final pushed correction requires a fresh full CI matrix before promotion."
  "2026-10-25T07:10:31.684Z",codex-agent,"Round-2 review reopened oracle correctness: replace seed-prefix/final-return checks with an exact transaction-owned PRE/POST oracle, and pair recovery cuts by observed journal commit phase instead of syscall ordinal. Add independent data-loss mutation and phase-equivalence controls, keep main history byte prefixes, and require fresh full release CI. Prior receipts remain historical and are superseded for these claims."
  "2026-10-25T07:22:44.290Z",codex-agent,"Oracle correction and independent revert proofs: exactState compares the complete canonical inventory, all item bytes, every full history stream and pending journals against the phase-selected clean reference after restart and after return. PRE/POST selection is made from successful native journal publication or published item publication in the interrupted trace, including resumed calls; final returns now perform an actual priority change. Restoring seed-history-prefix-only acceptance fails the real-state mutation regressions and the live exit-zero item-deletion/event-truncation regressions (exit 1); restoring exact equality passes (exit 0). Restoring same-syscall/same-ordinal pairing fails phase parity (exit 1); restoring phase matching passes (exit 0). Applicable patches and both tables are in docs/controls/crash-oracle and docs/CRASH_ORACLE_2026_10_25.json. Core mutation table: four mutations times six real acknowledged states plus one live restart and one live return each, 32 killed and zero survived. Fresh public copy: 85 items, 176 files, 26 kills, 24 exact restart/return successes, two published history-open divergences, two minimized fixtures, unchanged source. Phase parity: 20 same-phase pairs, 10 pass, 10 differences all explained by those two independently failing published cases; no ordinal-alias false failures. All 26 seed acknowledgements/history prefixes remain preserved. Default pinned strict health passes; optional full audit retains the two main-identical bj7a/unih mismatches, untouched. Running the full linked harness and fresh CI next."
  "2026-10-25T07:26:30.802Z",codex-agent,"Linked full harness validation passed: pm test --run --match test-concurrency=1 --progress --json ran node --test --test-concurrency=1 scripts/crash-*.test.mts, 50/50 passing with zero failures, skips or cancellations in 171 seconds. Strict TypeScript and ESLint pass. Removed the unused legacy permissive recoveredState helper so the active and unit-tested recovery path has one exact oracle; its replacement history-state regression also passes independently. Both live rename-1 cases now pass under different phases and are explicitly excluded from same-phase pairing. All 86 main streams remain raw byte prefixes; changed-history release gate passes. Default isolated pinned strict health passes; full audit remains blocked only on the two unchanged main items already recorded. Fresh full npm/Bun native release CI is still required on the pushed head."
